  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Immediate Lifesaving Emergency Shelter, Non-food Items (NFI) and Camp Coordination and Camp Management Assistance in Response to Tropical Cyclone Freddy&#x2019;s Impact</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Freddy made landfall in Malawi&#x2019;s Southern Region on 12 March 2023, bringing torrential rainfall, and causing devasting floods and mudslides in Southern Malawi. Critical infrastructure (roads, houses, hospitals) has been damaged and destroyed. As of 20 March 2023, Department of Disaster Management Affairs (DoDMA) estimates over 508,000 people have been displaced across the country to an estimated 534 evacuation centers/Internally Displaced People (IDP) sites. The International Organization for Migration (IOM) is upscaling the provision of Emergency Shelter and Non-Food Item (NFI) assistance, seeking to reach at least 12,900 vulnerable individuals with shelter kits, the construction of communal emergency shelters, site improvement and communal services. IOM is also scaling up Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) support to help coordinate the provision of emergency assistance and protection to IDPs settled in temporary sites. CCCM activities aim at supporting at least 20 camps, estimated at reaching around 16,000 IDPs located in camps.</narrative>
  </description>
